<!-- LINE ITEMS — a receipt's item table.
     ⚠ A REAL mj-include, unlike most content blocks: the `{{#each items}}` loop is RENDER-TIME
     Handlebars, not a compile-time parameter, so the enclosing template supplies `items` at send time
     and the include needs no arguments. Any template that declares
     `items: { of: { name, quantity, unitPrice, lineTotal } }` can use it.

     ⚠ TABLE-BASED (mj-table → a real <table>), which is what survives the Word engine — a receipt is
     the one place a data table is genuinely the right structure, and it holds up where a div grid
     would not. ⚠ Money and quantity arrive PRE-FORMATTED as strings (FR-048): "2", "$7.80". The
     template never formats a number.

     ⚠ Every cell carries `class="e-ink"`/`"e-muted"` so the dark-mode restatement reaches it — the
     dark rules target the ELEMENT, and a bare <td> would stay light-mode near-black on a dark ground.
     Each cell also states its own colour inline, so the message is correct with no stylesheet at all
     (contract §4).

     ⚠ 052 ADDED THE UNIT PRICE, on its own line under the name rather than in a third column. Three
     money columns at 600px wraps the product name to two or three ragged lines on a phone, which is
     where most of these are read; stacking keeps one row per item at every width. It is what makes a
     line CHECKABLE — "$9.50 each × 2 = $19.00" — rather than merely stated (FR-003). -->
<mj-table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="100%" css-class="e-ink"
          font-family="'General Sans', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif">
  {{#each items}}
  <tr>
    <td class="e-ink" style="padding:10px 0 2px 0;color:#1a1a1a;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;mso-line-height-rule:exactly;">{{name}}</td>
    <td class="e-ink" align="right" valign="top" style="padding:10px 0 2px 16px;color:#1a1a1a;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;mso-line-height-rule:exactly;white-space:nowrap;font-weight:600;">{{lineTotal}}</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="e-muted" colspan="2" style="padding:0 0 10px 0;color:#666666;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;mso-line-height-rule:exactly;">{{unitPrice}} each &middot; Qty {{quantity}}</td>
  </tr>
  {{/each}}
</mj-table>
